        "by": "micky-mickardo",
        "date": "2025-11-15",
        "text": "So during my time in Europe this year I decided I’d focus on nature and a more cutesy little towns and cities. Bern was a great stopping point because not only is it very beautiful, we were able to take a bunch of day trips,  to lauterbrunnen, interlocken and some more.\n\nThings you do \n• Nature is good around there accessible hikes\n• highly recommend day trips to hike around lauterbrunnen or paraglide in interlacken, unmatched views \n• I had fun renting bikes and seeing the city that way along with getting a nice workout in, we went for about 90km around the city and into the nature through some nice bike paths\n•it’s tradition for people to commute through the river, they jump on one end and come out where they need to, then there are showers for them to go to work or wherever they need to go after",
